@page "/mentor/projects/{Id:int}"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Mentor + "," + Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IMentorProjectsService MentorService
@inject IRoadmapStagesService RoadmapService
@inject IMentorWorkspaceService Workspace
@inject NavigationManager Nav

@*
    ── מרחב הפרויקט ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    VISUAL SOURCE OF TRUTH:  Motiva Mentor Project.dc.html (Claude Design).
                             Header, the four overview tiles, the stage strip,
                             the attention/work pair at 1 : 1.35, and the
                             meetings/activity pair are all that file's.
    ONE REAL PROJECT.        The reference ships five demo teams behind a
                             `?team=` prop. Not one of them is rendered here:
                             the route parameter names a real project and the
                             server refuses it unless this user is in
                             ProjectMentors for it (MentorController
                             GetProjectDetail → Forbid), which is why an
                             unauthorised id resolves to null and this page
                             says so instead of drawing anything.

    WHERE EVERY BLOCK'S DATA COMES FROM — all existing endpoints, no new ones:
      header / members / milestones / tasks / pending submissions
                        GET api/mentor/projects/{id}
      stage + % + next  GET api/roadmap-stages/projects/{id}/progress
                        (Overdue ?? Upcoming — the same precedence ציר
                        התקדמות uses), falling back to the project's own
                        milestone list when a cycle has no stages configured
      attention         the shared mentor snapshot, filtered to this project
      requests          the same snapshot's request list, filtered likewise
      last meeting      the project's own past personal tasks that carry an
                        hour — see LastMeetingLabel. The dated view that
                        MentorWorkspaceService.BuildCalendarAsync composed is
                        gone with the מועדים קרובים card: every date this page
                        still shows is on the row it belongs to (a milestone
                        on the strip, a deliverable in הגשות, a task in
                        משימות), so the composer had no consumer left and the
                        page no longer pays for it on load.

    פעילות אחרונה IS NOW A POSTSCRIPT, AND SMALLER THAN IT WAS. It used to
    open with "בקשה נפתחה — X" for every request on the project; every one of
    those is a row in the בקשות section, with its own status and its own
    filing date on it, a few hundred pixels up the same page. A feed whose
    top half restates the section above it is not a feed. What is left is what
    nothing else on this page states: a submission ARRIVING (who filed it and
    when — the sections carry the deliverable's state, never its author), a
    request MOVING after it was opened, and a guidance meeting that has
    already happened. The product still has no activity log — Notifications
    carry no ProjectId, milestones store no completion timestamp, a task
    stores no created-at — so nothing was invented to fill the gap; the block
    simply got shorter, lost its card, and disappears entirely when a project
    has none of the three.

    THE VERSION COLUMN IS NOT DRAWN, for the same reason: MentorTaskDto carries
    the latest submission's STATUS but no round number, and the round count
    lives one call deeper, inside the review surface that already shows it.

    THE REVIEW FLOW IS UNCHANGED — GET api/mentor/submissions/{id}/context and
    PATCH api/task-submissions/{id}/mentor-review, with the same round history
    and the same return-requires-a-note rule. What changed is the shell it is
    drawn in: it is PwDetail now, the same surface a request opens in, rather
    than an edge-attached drawer of its own. The ?submissionId= deep link the
    calendar sends still opens it.
*@

@*  ══ The two detail surfaces this workspace opens ═══════════════════════

    BOTH ARE PwDetail. A submission review and a request used to open two
    unrelated things: an edge-attached drawer with its own header, section
    rules and button vocabulary, and a block that grew inside the work list
    between two rows that carried on as if nothing had happened. One surface
    now, one hierarchy — eyebrow, title, status, who and when, then the
    content, the files, the trail and the viewer's own action.

    THE FLOWS ARE UNTOUCHED. The review is still
    GET api/mentor/submissions/{id}/context and
    PATCH api/task-submissions/{id}/mentor-review, with the same round
    history and the same return-requires-a-note rule; the request is still
    MentorRequestDetail with the same one recommendation POST. Only the shell
    around them changed.
*@

@if (_reviewOpen)
{
    <PwDetail IsOpen="true"
              Loading="@_reviewLoading"
              LoadingLabel="טוענת פרטי הגשה…"
              Eyebrow="@_reviewCtx?.MilestoneTitle"
              Title="@(_reviewCtx?.TaskTitle ?? "הגשה")"
              StatusText="@(_reviewCtx is null ? null : DrawerMentorStatusLabel(_reviewCtx.MentorStatus))"
              StatusTone="@(_reviewCtx is null ? PwTone.Quiet : ReviewTone(_reviewCtx.MentorStatus))"
              Meta="@ReviewMeta"
              OnClose="CloseDrawer">

        <Side>
            @if (_reviewCtx is not null)
            {
                @* ── What this mentor may do, and nothing else ── *@
                @if (_reviewCtx.MentorStatus == "Pending")
                {
                    <section class="pwd-sec pwd-sec-action">
                        <p class="pwd-sec-title">סקירת מנחה</p>

                        <div class="pwd-form">
                            <label class="pwd-label" for="mpw-review-note">
                                פידבק (נדרש בעת החזרה לתיקון)
                            </label>
                            <textarea id="mpw-review-note" class="pwd-textarea" rows="5"
                                      placeholder="הוסף הערות או הסברים לסטודנט…"
                                      value="@_reviewFeedback"
                                      @oninput="@((ChangeEventArgs e) => { _reviewFeedback = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty; if (_feedbackError.Length > 0) _feedbackError = string.Empty; })"
                                      disabled="@_reviewing"></textarea>

                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_feedbackError))
                            {
                                <p class="pwd-error" role="alert">@_feedbackError</p>
                            }
                            @if (_reviewError)
                            {
                                <p class="pwd-error" role="alert">שגיאה בשמירה. נסה שנית.</p>
                            }

                            <div class="pwd-actions pwd-actions-stack">
                                <button type="button" class="pwd-btn pwd-btn-approve"
                                        @onclick='() => SubmitReviewAsync("Approved")'
                                        disabled="@_reviewing">
                                    @(_reviewing && _pendingAction == "Approved" ? "שומרת…" : "אשר הגשה")
                                </button>
                                <button type="button" class="pwd-btn pwd-btn-return"
                                        @onclick='() => SubmitReviewAsync("Returned")'
                                        disabled="@_reviewing">
                                    @(_reviewing && _pendingAction == "Returned" ? "שומרת…" : "החזר לתיקון")
                                </button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                }
                else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewCtx.MentorFeedback))
                {
                    @*  THE VERDICT IS ALREADY IN THE HEADER. What this block
                        uniquely holds is the words that were written, so it is
                        drawn only when there are some. *@
                    <section class="pwd-sec pwd-sec-action">
                        <p class="pwd-sec-title">הערות שנכתבו לצוות</p>
                        <p class="pwd-text pwd-quote">@_reviewCtx.MentorFeedback</p>
                    </section>
                }
            }
        </Side>

        <ChildContent>
        @if (_reviewCtx is not null)
        {
            @* ── What was asked for ── *@
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewCtx.TaskDescription))
            {
                <section class="pwd-sec">
                    <p class="pwd-sec-title">תיאור המשימה</p>
                    <p class="pwd-text">@_reviewCtx.TaskDescription</p>
                </section>
            }

            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewCtx.Notes))
            {
                <section class="pwd-sec">
                    <p class="pwd-sec-title">הערות הסטודנט</p>
                    <p class="pwd-text pwd-quote">@_reviewCtx.Notes</p>
                </section>
            }

            @*  ── THE DELIVERABLE ITSELF ────────────────────────────────
                THE DRIVE LINK IS A FILE. Submissions have been Drive-link
                only since 2026-05-19, and this section listed `Files` alone
                — which is empty for every modern submission. So the surface
                whose whole purpose is reviewing a deliverable said
                "לא צורפו קבצים להגשה זו" while holding the URL of the
                deliverable in the very payload it was drawing. The link is
                the first row of this list now; the legacy uploads that still
                exist follow it.

                These are the SUBMISSION's files — not the project's shared
                materials (the workspace header) and not a request's
                attachments (that request's own surface). *@
            <section class="pwd-sec">
                <p class="pwd-sec-title">
                    קבצי ההגשה
                    @if (ReviewFileCount > 0)
                    {
                        <span class="pwd-count">@ReviewFileCount</span>
                    }
                </p>

                @if (ReviewFileCount == 0)
                {
                    <p class="pwd-empty">לא צורפו קבצים ולא נמסר קישור להגשה זו</p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="pwd-files">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewCtx.DriveUrl))
                        {
                            <a class="pwd-file pwd-file-drive" href="@_reviewCtx.DriveUrl"
                               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                <span class="pwd-file-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                                    <span class="oi oi-external-link"></span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="pwd-file-info">
                                    <span class="pwd-file-name">ההגשה ב-Google Drive</span>
                                    <span class="pwd-file-size">@HostOf(_reviewCtx.DriveUrl)</span>
                                </span>
                            </a>
                        }

                        @foreach (var f in _reviewCtx.Files)
                        {
                            <div class="pwd-file">
                                <span class="pwd-file-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                                    <span class="oi @FileIcon(f.ContentType)"></span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="pwd-file-info">
                                    <span class="pwd-file-name">@f.OriginalFileName</span>
                                    <span class="pwd-file-size">@FormatSize(f.SizeBytes)</span>
                                </span>
                                <a class="pwd-file-go"
                                   href="submissions/@f.StoredFileName"
                                   download="@f.OriginalFileName"
                                   title="הורדה">
                                    <span class="oi oi-cloud-download" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </section>

            @*  ── PREVIOUS ROUNDS, COLLAPSED ──────────────────────────
                The current round's notes and files are the section above —
                they are what the mentor is reviewing, not history. What is
                left here is the rounds that came BEFORE, which matter only
                when the reader goes looking, so they are a disclosure that
                states its own size and opens on demand.

                It used to render every round expanded-current-first inside
                the main column, so the surface opened on an accordion and
                the thing being reviewed was one item inside it. *@
            @if (PreviousRounds.Count > 0)
            {
                <details class="pwd-more">
                    <summary>
                        סבבים קודמים
                        <span class="pwd-count">@PreviousRounds.Count</span>
                        <span class="oi oi-chevron-bottom pwd-more-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    </summary>

                    <div class="pwd-more-body">
                        @foreach (var round in PreviousRounds)
                        {
                            <div class="pwd-round">
                                <div class="pwd-round-btn" role="group">
                                    <span class="pwd-round-start">
                                        <span class="pwd-round-num">סבב @round.RoundNumber</span>
                                        <span class="pwd-round-date">@round.SubmittedAt.IsraelFormat("dd/MM/yy HH:mm")</span>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="pwd-round-end">
                                        <span class="pwd-badge @ReviewToneClass(round.MentorStatus)">
                                            @DrawerMentorStatusLabel(round.MentorStatus)
                                        </span>
                                    </span>
                                </div>

                                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(round.MentorFeedback))
                                {
                                    <div class="pwd-round-body">
                                        <div class="pwd-fb pwd-fb-mentor">
                                            <span class="pwd-fb-head">
                                                <span class="oi oi-person" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                                פידבק מנחה
                                            </span>
                                            <p class="pwd-fb-text">@round.MentorFeedback</p>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                </details>
            }

        }
        </ChildContent>
    </PwDetail>
}

@*  ── One request, opened over the workspace ────────────────────────────
    The real request flow, unchanged: the same MentorRequestDetail the בקשות
    inbox draws, the same MarkRead and the same one recommendation POST. What
    changed is where it appears — a surface that names the request it is
    showing, instead of a block inside the list that named nothing. *@
@if (_openRequestId is int openReqId && RequestRow(openReqId) is { } openReq)
{
    <PwDetail IsOpen="true"
              Eyebrow="@RequestTypes.Label(openReq.RequestType)"
              Title="@openReq.Title"
              StatusText="@PwRequestVocabulary.StatusLabel(openReq.Status, ViewerOf(openReq))"
              StatusTone="@PwRequestVocabulary.Tone(openReq.Status, ViewerOf(openReq))"
              Meta="@RequestMeta(openReq)"
              OnClose="CloseRequest">
        <Side>
            <MentorRequestDetail RequestId="@openReqId"
                                 Layout="MentorRequestDetail.DetailLayout.Surface"
                                 Part="MentorRequestDetail.DetailPart.Action"
                                 ShowHeader="false"
                                 OnChanged="ReloadAsync" />
        </Side>

        <ChildContent>
            <MentorRequestDetail RequestId="@openReqId"
                                 Layout="MentorRequestDetail.DetailLayout.Surface"
                                 Part="MentorRequestDetail.DetailPart.Content"
                                 ShowHeader="false"
                                 OnChanged="ReloadAsync" />
        </ChildContent>
    </PwDetail>
}


<div class="mpw-page">

    @* ── Back to פרויקטים בהנחייתי ─────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <a class="mpw-back" href="mentor/projects">
        <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="2.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"></path>
        </svg>
        פרויקטים בהנחייתי
    </a>

    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת את מרחב הפרויקט…" />
    }
    else if (_detail is null)
    {
        <MEmptyState Live="true"
                     Title="הפרויקט לא נמצא או שאינך מנחה שלו"
                     Description="מרחב הפרויקט נפתח רק למנחה שמשויך אליו בפועל.">
            <Action>
                <MButton Variant="MButton.ButtonVariant.Secondary"
                         OnClick="@(() => Nav.NavigateTo("mentor/projects"))">
                    חזרה לפרויקטים בהנחייתי
                </MButton>
            </Action>
        </MEmptyState>
    }
    else
    {
        @* ── The shared workspace ───────────────────────────────────────────

            THE COMPOSITION MOVED, THE MENTOR'S WORK DID NOT. Identity, the
            stage strip, the attention/work pair and the dates/activity pair are
            now <ProjectWorkspace/> — the same component and the same stylesheet
            the lecturer's מרחב הפרויקט draws, so one project cannot be laid out
            two ways depending on who opened it.

            Everything this page actually DOES stayed here: the review surface
            and the request surface above, the shared task editor, the deep
            links and every routing rule in OpenAttentionItemAsync /
            OpenActivityAsync. The component raises a row's key and this file
            decides what opens.

            THE FOUR OVERVIEW TILES ARE GONE. שלב נוכחי is the header's own
            subtitle, אבן דרך הבאה is the strip directly beneath it, and
            סטטוס הפרויקט is the badge beside the title — cards restating
            things already on the screen.

            THE MEETING SCHEDULER MOVED, IT DID NOT GO. קביעת פגישת הנחיה and
            the "last meeting" line used to sit under מועדים קרובים; that card
            is gone, and they are now in the header beside the project's other
            controls, which is where a project-level action belongs. Same
            button, same modal, same POST.
        *@
        @* CONTEXT IS THE ROUTE, not the role list. This file is only ever
           reached through /mentor/projects/{id}, so it declares Mentor
           unconditionally — a dual-role account (Staff + Mentor) that arrives
           here from פרויקטים בהנחייתי gets the mentor's workspace even though
           RoleService.IsAdminOrStaff would also answer true for them, and the
           mentor vocabulary below ("דורש את פעולתך", "בבדיקת מרצה") is
           correct for that reader. *@
        <ProjectWorkspace View="@View"
                          Context="PwContext.Mentor"
                          OnWorkRowClick="OnWorkKeyAsync"
                          OnActivityClick="OnActivityKeyAsync">

            <IdentityActions>
                @* The mentor's own project control, in the identity area.

                   GATED ON MENTORING THIS PROJECT, not on holding the Mentor
                   role. MentorPersonalTaskModal below is mounted only when
                   _summary resolves — i.e. when api/mentor/projects, which is
                   ProjectMentors-scoped, actually returned this project — so
                   for anyone else the button was already inert: it set a flag
                   for a modal that was never rendered. Staff and Admin can
                   open this route (MentorController lets them), and that is
                   exactly the account this dead control was shown to. *@
                @if (IsProjectMentor)
                {
                    <button type="button" class="mpw-schedule motiva-cta" @onclick="OpenScheduler">
                        <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                             stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                            <path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path>
                        </svg>
                        קביעת פגישת הנחיה
                    </button>
                    <span class="mpw-last-meeting">@LastMeetingLabel</span>
                }
                else if (CanUseLecturerWorkspace)
                {
                    @* Staff who do not mentor this project. Every mentor feed
                       on this page is ProjectMentors-scoped and answers empty
                       for them, so say which workspace they are in and where
                       their own one is, rather than letting an empty mentor
                       page read as "this project has nothing happening". *@
                    <span class="mpw-not-mentor">אינך המנחה של פרויקט זה</span>
                    <a class="mpw-to-lecturer" href="@($"projects/{Id}/overview")">
                        למרחב הפרויקט שלך
                    </a>
                }
            </IdentityActions>

        </ProjectWorkspace>
    }
</div>

@* ── קביעת פגישת הנחיה / עריכת משימה אישית ────────────────────────────────
    The mentor calendar's own editor, opened here with this project already
    chosen. Not a second create flow: same component, same POST, same Google
    sync — the only thing this page supplies is the project the mentor is
    already looking at, and the select stays editable.

    It EDITS as well as creates now, so a personal task on this page — in
    the משימות tab or the activity list — opens its
    editor here instead of sending the mentor to /mentor/tasks?editTask= to
    meet the very same modal on another screen. *@
@if (_summary is not null)
{
    <MentorPersonalTaskModal IsOpen="@(_scheduleOpen || _editingTask is not null)"
                             EditingTask="@_editingTask"
                             Projects="@(new[] { _summary })"
                             InitialProjectId="@Id"
                             OnClose="CloseTaskModal"
                             OnSaved="OnMeetingSavedAsync"
                             OnDeleted="@(_ => OnTaskRemovedAsync())" />
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Id { get; set; }
    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }

    // ── Loaded payloads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    private MentorProjectDetailDto?    _detail;
    private ProjectRoadmapProgressDto? _roadmap;
    private MentorWorkspace            _ws = MentorWorkspace.Empty;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// Does the CURRENT USER actually mentor this project?
    ///
    /// <para>Not "do they hold the Mentor role" — a dual-role account holds it
    /// on every project, including ones it only supervises as staff. This
    /// reads the ProjectMentors-scoped list the workspace snapshot already
    /// carries, so it answers the question the mentor surfaces actually
    /// depend on: <see cref="_summary"/> is non-null exactly when
    /// api/mentor/projects returned this project for this caller.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>It is the same condition that mounts MentorPersonalTaskModal, so
    /// the scheduler button and the modal it opens can no longer disagree.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private bool IsProjectMentor => _summary is not null;

    /// <summary>
    /// What this reader may do with ONE request, as the server answered it.
    ///
    /// <para>Per row, not per page: the capability depends on the request as
    /// much as on the reader — its mentor stage, its lecturer decision, whether
    /// it is closed. The row payload carries the answer
    /// (ExtensionWorkflow.Resolve, server-side), and this only puts it in the
    /// shape the shared vocabulary reads. The lecturer workspace builds the
    /// identical record from its own rows, so one request reads consistently on
    /// both pages.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private PwRequestViewer ViewerOf(ProjectRequestRowDto r) => new(
        IsStaff:             RoleService.IsAdminOrStaff(_user),
        CanRecommend:        r.ViewerCanRecommend,
        CanDecide:           r.ViewerCanDecide,
        MentorStageComplete: r.MentorStageComplete,
        // Server-set from ProjectMentors, per request, by the same
        // ApplyCapabilities that writes the two flags above — so a request
        // awaiting SOME OTHER project's mentor stays false here. Without it the
        // vocabulary cannot tell "waiting on a mentor" from "waiting on you",
        // because Resolve zeroes both capabilities for non-extension types.
        IsProjectMentor:     r.ViewerIsProjectMentor);

    /// <summary>Staff and Admin have a lecturer workspace for this project to
    /// be pointed at; a plain mentor does not, so they are told nothing rather
    /// than offered a route that would only degrade.</summary>
    private bool CanUseLecturerWorkspace => RoleService.IsAdminOrStaff(_user);

    // ── Projections onto THIS project ───────────────────────────────────────
    // Every one of these is a filter over a snapshot the whole mentor
    // experience already shares. Nothing is re-fetched per section and nothing
    // is recomputed — an item waiting here is the same row, with the same
    // wording and the same age, that בית and המשימות שלי draw.
    private MentorProjectSummaryDto?         _summary;
    private List<MentorAttentionItemDto>     _attention = new();
    private List<ProjectRequestRowDto>       _requests  = new();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto>            _personal  = new();

    // ── Local UI state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The three keys used to name TABS; they now name the three SECTIONS, all
    // of which are on the page at once. Nothing selects between them any more,
    // so there is no open-tab state and no ?tab= deep link to honour — a link
    // that used to say "land on בקשות" lands on a page where בקשות is already
    // visible.
    private const string SecSubs  = "subs";
    private const string SecReqs  = "reqs";
    private const string SecTasks = "tasks";

    /// <summary>The request whose detail surface is open, or null. It is also
    /// what marks the row it came from while the surface covers the page.</summary>
    private int? _openRequestId;

    private bool   _scheduleOpen;

    /// <summary>The personal task being edited in the shared modal, or null.
    /// Separate from <see cref="_scheduleOpen"/> because that one CREATES a
    /// meeting on this project and this one opens an existing row.</summary>
    private PersonalTaskDto? _editingTask;

    // ── Review surface state (same flow, new shell) ─────────────────────────

    /// <summary>Whether the review surface is mounted. Separate from
    /// <see cref="_reviewCtx"/> because the context arrives one round-trip
    /// later: the old drawer rendered only when the context was already
    /// present, so its own loading state could never be seen.</summary>
    private bool                        _reviewOpen;
    private MentorSubmissionContextDto? _reviewCtx;
    private bool                        _reviewLoading;
    private bool                        _reviewing;
    private bool                        _reviewError;
    /// <summary>Validation-specific error shown when "Return" is clicked
    /// without a non-empty feedback note. Cleared on any feedback edit.</summary>
    private string                      _feedbackError  = "";
    private string                      _reviewFeedback = "";
    private string                      _pendingAction  = "";

    /// <summary>Every round EXCEPT the one being reviewed. The current
    /// round's own notes and files are drawn as content, not as history —
    /// they are the thing the mentor opened this surface to look at.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MentorSubmissionRoundDto> PreviousRounds =>
        _reviewCtx is null
            ? Array.Empty<MentorSubmissionRoundDto>()
            : _reviewCtx.History.Where(r => r.SubmissionId != _reviewCtx.SubmissionId).ToList();

    /// <summary>A URL's host, for a file row's second line — "drive.google.com"
    /// tells a reader where a link goes; the full URL just overflows.</summary>
    private static string HostOf(string? url) =>
        Uri.TryCreate(url, UriKind.Absolute, out var u) ? u.Host : "";

    // ── Load ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await LoadAsync();

        // ?submissionId= — the calendar's Review deep link.
        //
        // Opened only AFTER the project detail resolved, because a null _detail
        // means this mentor is not authorized for this project and nothing here
        // should open. GetSubmissionContextAsync is itself mentor-scoped
        // server-side, so a crafted submission id from another project answers
        // null and the drawer simply does not appear — this parameter grants no
        // access of its own, it only saves a click on a page already allowed.
        if (_detail is not null && int.TryParse(QueryValue("submissionId"), out var deepLinkSubmissionId))
            await OpenReviewDrawer(deepLinkSubmissionId);

        // ?requestId= — the same courtesy for a request notification. It opens
        // the request's own surface now rather than selecting a tab and
        // expanding a row inside it.
        if (_detail is not null && int.TryParse(QueryValue("requestId"), out var deepLinkRequestId)
            && _requests.Any(r => r.Id == deepLinkRequestId))
        {
            _openRequestId = deepLinkRequestId;
        }
    }

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;

        // Three independent round-trips, concurrently. The snapshot is the one
        // every mentor screen shares; the other two are this project's own.
        var detailTask  = MentorService.GetProjectDetailAsync(Id);
        var roadmapTask = RoadmapService.GetProjectProgressAsync(Id);
        var wsTask      = Workspace.LoadAsync();
        await Task.WhenAll(detailTask, roadmapTask, wsTask);

        _detail  = await detailTask;
        _roadmap = await roadmapTask;
        _ws      = await wsTask;

        _summary   = _ws.Projects.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Id == Id);
        _attention = _ws.Attention.Items.Where(i => i.ProjectId == Id).ToList();
        _requests  = _ws.Requests.Where(r => r.ProjectId == Id)
                                 .OrderByDescending(r => r.UpdatedAt)
                                 .ToList();
        _personal  = _ws.PersonalTasks.Where(t => t.ProjectId == Id).ToList();

        _isLoading = false;
    }

    /// <summary>A recommendation was accepted or a meeting was saved, so counts
    /// and dates have moved — reload rather than patching rows by hand.</summary>
    private async Task ReloadAsync()
    {
        _openRequestId = null;
        await LoadAsync();
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    // ── Header, tiles and stage ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>The project's single attention signal — the SAME vocabulary
    /// פרויקטים בהנחייתי sorts and colours its list by, read off the same three
    /// facts, so the row there and the chip here can never disagree.</summary>
    private MentorProjectSignal Signal => MentorProjectSignals.Of(
        milestoneOverdue: MentorTime.IsOverdue(NextDue),
        pendingReviews:   _attention.Count(i => i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Submission),
        openRequests:     _ws.OpenRequestsFor(Id));

    private StageProgressDto? CurrentStage =>
        _roadmap?.Stages.FirstOrDefault(s => s.Status == RoadmapStageStatuses.Current);

    /// <summary>The first milestone the team has not finished — the fallback for
    /// every "current / next" question when a cycle has no roadmap stages
    /// configured, and the same row the projects list falls back to.</summary>
    private MentorMilestoneDto? FirstOpenMilestone =>
        _detail?.Milestones.FirstOrDefault(m => m.Status is not ("Completed" or "Done"));

    private string StageName =>
        CurrentStage?.Name
        ?? FirstOpenMilestone?.Title
        ?? "טרם החל";

    /// <summary>Overdue outranks upcoming — the same precedence ציר התקדמות
    /// renders, so the two screens name the same milestone as "the next one".</summary>
    private UpcomingMilestoneDto? NextMilestone => _roadmap?.Overdue ?? _roadmap?.Upcoming;

    /// <summary>Still the input to <see cref="Signal"/>. The title and the next
    /// meeting that sat beside it fed the four overview tiles, which the stage
    /// strip and the dates card now say for themselves.</summary>
    private DateTime? NextDue =>
        NextMilestone is not null ? NextMilestone.DueDate : FirstOpenMilestone?.DueDate;

    // ── The view handed to ProjectWorkspace ─────────────────────────────────
    //
    // A PROJECTION, NOT A SECOND MODEL. Every list below is one of this page's
    // existing computed properties — Submissions, WorkTasks, UpcomingDates,
    // Activity, _attention, _requests — mapped onto the shared row shapes.
    // Not one rule about what belongs in a list, how it is ordered, how it is
    // worded or how long it has waited moved or changed; only the type it is
    // handed over in did.

    private ProjectWorkspaceView View
    {
        get
        {
            var stages = PwStages.Build(_roadmap, MilestonesLite);

            return new ProjectWorkspaceView(
                Identity:           Identity,
                Stages:             stages,
                StagesSummary:      PwStages.Summary(stages),
                StagesEmptyText:    "לא הוגדרו אבני דרך לפרויקט זה.",
                Sections:           Sections,
                Activity:           ActivityRows);
        }
    }

    private PwIdentity Identity => new(
        Title:         _detail!.Title,
        // A project with no team row yet still has an identity line to draw;
        // its number is the name everyone already uses for it.
        TeamName:      string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_detail.TeamName)
                           ? $"צוות {_detail.ProjectNumber}"
                           : _detail.TeamName,
        StageName:     StageName,
        // Milestone completion — the headline progress on both workspaces.
        ProgressPct:   _detail.MilestoneProgressPct,
        StatusText:    MentorProjectSignals.HealthLabel(Signal),
        StatusVariant: MentorProjectSignals.HealthVariant(Signal),
        Members:       _detail.TeamMembers.Select(m => $"{m.FullName} · {m.Email}").ToList(),
        Meta:          Array.Empty<PwMeta>(),
        // The team's own ProjectResources, read-only — see PwMaterials.
        Materials:     PwMaterials.From(_detail.Resources));

    /// <summary>The project's milestones in the shape the shared stage builder
    /// reads, for the cycles that configure no roadmap stages.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PwMilestoneLite> MilestonesLite =>
        (_detail?.Milestones ?? new List<MentorMilestoneDto>())
            .Select(m => new PwMilestoneLite(
                m.ProjectMilestoneId, m.Title, m.OrderIndex, m.Status, m.DueDate))
            .ToList();

    // ── Work ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// THE THREE SECTIONS, in the order the questions are asked, each carrying
    /// only what a mentor can act on plus a little orientation.
    ///
    /// <para>The rows and their wording are unchanged; what each row now also
    /// declares is its <see cref="PwRowRank"/>, derived from the very predicate
    /// that already decided its label and its tone. Nothing new is computed,
    /// and nothing that used to be reachable stopped being reachable — the
    /// dormant rows are behind the section's own "לכל…".</para>
    ///
    /// <para>The order is fixed and never moves with the data. A section that
    /// changed places when its counts changed would make the page
    /// unlearnable.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PwSection> Sections
    {
        get
        {
            var subs  = Submissions;
            var tasks = WorkTasks;

            int pendingReviews = subs.Count(s => s.SubmissionId is not null);
            int missing        = subs.Count(s => s is { Submitted: false, Overdue: true });
            int submitted      = subs.Count(s => s.Submitted);
            int openRequests   = _requests.Count(r => MentorRequestBuckets.Of(r.Status) != MentorRequestBucket.Closed);
            int actionable     = _requests.Count(r => PwRequestVocabulary.OwnedByViewer(r.Status, ViewerOf(r)));
            int overdueTasks   = tasks.Count(t => t.Overdue);

            return new[]
            {
                new PwSection(SecSubs, "הגשות", "oi-inbox",
                    Rows:      subs.Select((s, i) => new PwWorkRow(
                                    Key:             s.SubmissionId is int id ? $"review:{id}" : $"subrow:{i}",
                                    Title:           s.Title,
                                    // The context line — which milestone this
                                    // deliverable belongs to. The deadline still
                                    // reaches the row only when it was MISSED: a
                                    // date that was met is not news, and one that
                                    // has not arrived is why the row is dormant.
                                    Meta:            s.Milestone,
                                    Trailing:        s.Overdue ? s.Due : null,
                                    TrailingLate:    s.Overdue,
                                    State:           s.State,
                                    StateTone:       ToneOf(s.StateClass),
                                    ActionLabel:     s.SubmissionId is not null ? "לבדיקה" : null,
                                    ActionIsPrimary: s.SubmissionId is not null,
                                    IsClickable:     s.SubmissionId is not null,
                                    // `s.SubmissionId is int` FIRST: without it a
                                    // row that has no pending round (null) matches
                                    // the null _reviewCtx of a surface that is still
                                    // loading, and every unclickable row lights up.
                                    IsOpen:          _reviewOpen && s.SubmissionId is int openSub
                                                     && _reviewCtx?.SubmissionId == openSub,
                                    Rank:            SubmissionRank(s))).ToList(),
                    EmptyText: "אין משימות הגשה בפרויקט זה",
                    // What the card says INSTEAD of rows when nothing is
                    // outstanding: the settled position, in one line.
                    Summary:     pendingReviews > 0
                                     ? PwCount.Phrase(pendingReviews,
                                           "הגשה אחת ממתינה לבדיקתך", "{0} הגשות ממתינות לבדיקתך")
                                     : missing > 0
                                         ? PwCount.Phrase(missing, "הגשה אחת חסרה", "{0} הגשות חסרות")
                                         : $"{submitted} מתוך {subs.Count} הוגשו",
                    // Matches the lecturer's הגשות summary exactly: the
                    // reader's own queue is Attention, a missing deliverable is
                    // the genuine negative.
                    SummaryTone: pendingReviews > 0 ? PwTone.Attention
                                 : missing > 0      ? PwTone.Late
                                 :                    PwTone.Quiet,
                    AllHref:     MentorLinks.Reviews,
                    AllLabel:    "לתור ההגשות",
                    MoreLabel:   "לכל ההגשות"),

                new PwSection(SecReqs, "בקשות", "oi-envelope-closed",
                    Rows:      _requests.Select(r =>
                               {
                                   // ONE ANSWER, FROM THE SERVER. The button, the
                                   // tone, the rank and the status wording all read
                                   // the capability ExtensionWorkflow.Resolve
                                   // computed for this caller and this request —
                                   // the same one /extension/decision gates on.
                                   var v   = ViewerOf(r);
                                   var cta = PwRequestVocabulary.ActionLabel(r.Status, v);

                                   return new PwWorkRow(
                                       Key:             $"req:{r.Id}",
                                       Title:           r.Title,
                                       // Who asked, on the context line; when they
                                       // asked, at the row's end.
                                       Meta:            r.CreatedByName,
                                       Trailing:        r.CreatedAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("dd.MM"),
                                       // OWNERSHIP, NOT VISIBILITY — the same
                                       // resolver the lecturer workspace uses.
                                       State:           PwRequestVocabulary.StatusLabel(r.Status, v),
                                       StateTone:       PwRequestVocabulary.Tone(r.Status, v),
                                       ActionLabel:     cta,
                                       ActionIsPrimary: cta is not null,
                                       IsClickable:     true,
                                       IsOpen:          _openRequestId == r.Id,
                                       Rank:            RequestRank(r));
                               }).ToList(),
                    EmptyText:   "אין בקשות בפרויקט זה",
                    Summary:     actionable > 0
                                     ? PwCount.Phrase(actionable, "בקשה אחת ממתינה לך", "{0} בקשות ממתינות לך")
                                     : openRequests > 0
                                         ? PwCount.Phrase(openRequests, "בקשה אחת פתוחה", "{0} בקשות פתוחות")
                                         : "אין בקשות פתוחות",
                    SummaryTone: actionable > 0 ? PwTone.Attention : PwTone.Quiet,
                    AllHref:     MentorLinks.RequestsInbox,
                    AllLabel:    "לכל הבקשות",
                    MoreLabel:   "לכל בקשות הפרויקט"),

                new PwSection(SecTasks, "משימות", "oi-task",
                    Rows:      tasks.Select((k, i) => new PwWorkRow(
                                    Key:          k.Task is PersonalTaskDto own ? $"ptask:{own.Id}" : $"teamtask:{i}",
                                    Title:        k.Title,
                                    // WHO, and nothing else. The "שלי / צוות" chip
                                    // said the same thing this line already says —
                                    // a mentor's own row reads "משימה שלך" — so one
                                    // of the two ownership signals went.
                                    Meta:         k.Assignee,
                                    Trailing:     k.Overdue ? k.Due : null,
                                    TrailingLate: k.Overdue,
                                    State:        k.State,
                                    StateTone:    ToneOf(k.StateClass),
                                    // Only the mentor's OWN task has an editor here;
                                    // a team task stays unclickable, as it always was.
                                    IsClickable:  k.Task is not null,
                                    Rank:         TaskRank(k))).ToList(),
                    EmptyText:   "אין משימות פתוחות בפרויקט זה",
                    Summary:     overdueTasks > 0
                                     ? PwCount.Phrase(overdueTasks, "משימה אחת באיחור", "{0} משימות באיחור")
                                     : PwCount.Phrase(tasks.Count, "משימה אחת פתוחה", "{0} משימות פתוחות"),
                    SummaryTone: overdueTasks > 0 ? PwTone.Late : PwTone.Quiet,
                    MoreLabel:   "לכל המשימות",
                    Note:        $"{_detail!.CompletedTasks} מתוך {_detail.TotalTasks} משימות הושלמו"),
            };
        }
    }

    // ── Rank: the same three predicates, read once more ─────────────────────
    //
    // Each of these reads the fact the row's own label already states. They add
    // no rule about the workflow — they only answer "does a mentor need to see
    // this today", and the answer decides prominence, not permission.

    /// <summary>A deliverable is the mentor's when a round is pending review;
    /// it is an exception when its deadline passed and nothing was handed in;
    /// it is context once it has been handed in at all. A deliverable whose
    /// date has not arrived and which nobody has touched is dormant — that is
    /// the majority of every project, and drawing it was most of the noise.</summary>
    private static PwRowRank SubmissionRank(SubRow s) =>
        s.SubmissionId is not null   ? PwRowRank.Waiting
        : s is { Submitted: false, Overdue: true } ? PwRowRank.Exception
        : s.Submitted                ? PwRowRank.Context
        :                              PwRowRank.Dormant;

    /// <summary>The next move is this viewer's, or it is not — the same
    /// ownership answer the row's own status label gives. Anything still open
    /// sits with somebody else and is context; a closed request is history and
    /// waits behind "לכל בקשות הפרויקט".</summary>
    private PwRowRank RequestRank(ProjectRequestRowDto r) =>
        PwRequestVocabulary.OwnedByViewer(r.Status, ViewerOf(r))          ? PwRowRank.Waiting
        : MentorRequestBuckets.Of(r.Status) != MentorRequestBucket.Closed ? PwRowRank.Context
        :                                                                   PwRowRank.Dormant;

    /// <summary>Late is the exception, whoever owns it — that is what a
    /// supervisor scans this list for. Work actually under way, and the
    /// mentor's own open items, are context. A task nobody has started and
    /// which is not late requires nothing from anyone.</summary>
    private static PwRowRank TaskRank(WorkTaskRow k) =>
        k.Overdue                                       ? PwRowRank.Exception
        : k.IsMine                                      ? PwRowRank.Context
        : k.StateClass is "mpw-state-blue" or "mpw-state-violet" ? PwRowRank.Context
        :                                                 PwRowRank.Dormant;

    /// <summary>The mpw- state class this page already computed, read back as
    /// the shared tone. Kept as a translation rather than replacing the two
    /// state-class helpers, so the rules that DECIDE a state stay exactly where
    /// and as they were.</summary>
    /// <summary>
    /// The legacy state keys, mapped onto the shared semantic vocabulary.
    ///
    /// <para>The keys are colour names from the page this component replaced
    /// and are kept only as identifiers; what each one MEANS is decided here,
    /// once, and it now agrees with the lecturer's copy of the same rows:
    /// blue and violet were both "in flight with somebody else" (הוגש,
    /// הוחזר לתיקון) and both resolve to Waiting; `mpw-state-attention` is the
    /// reader's own queue.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static PwTone ToneOf(string stateClass) => stateClass switch
    {
        "mpw-state-attention" => PwTone.Attention,
        "mpw-state-teal"      => PwTone.Done,
        "mpw-state-blue"      => PwTone.Waiting,
        "mpw-state-violet"    => PwTone.Waiting,
        "mpw-late"            => PwTone.Late,
        _                     => PwTone.Quiet,
    };

    // ── Activity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private IReadOnlyList<PwActivityRow> ActivityRows =>
        Activity.Select((v, i) => new PwActivityRow(
            Key:         $"act:{i}",
            Text:        v.Text,
            Meta:        v.Meta,
            Tone:        ActivityTone(v.ToneClass),
            IsClickable: true)).ToList();

    /// <summary>
    /// Activity dots, in the shared vocabulary.
    ///
    /// <para>An activity feed reports what already happened; it asks the reader
    /// for nothing, so violet and blue — two brand hues in the Motiva scope,
    /// spent on "an event exists" — both resolve to Quiet. The lecturer's copy
    /// of this feed made the same change. Teal survives because a completion IS
    /// a state worth marking, and it is the same teal every other Lecturer and
    /// Mentor screen uses for one.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static PwTone ActivityTone(string toneClass) => toneClass switch
    {
        "mpw-dot-teal" => PwTone.Done,
        _              => PwTone.Quiet,
    };

    // ── Row keys → this page's own routing ──────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The shared component knows nothing about a review drawer, a request
    // accordion or a task editor: it raises the key the row was built with and
    // these four methods hand it to the handler that already existed.

    /// <summary>The integer after "prefix:" in a row key, or null.</summary>
    private static int? KeyId(string key, string prefix) =>
        key.StartsWith(prefix + ":", StringComparison.Ordinal)
        && int.TryParse(key.AsSpan(prefix.Length + 1), out var id)
            ? id : null;

    private async Task OnWorkKeyAsync(string key)
    {
        if (KeyId(key, "review") is int submissionId)
        {
            await OpenReviewDrawer(submissionId);
            return;
        }

        if (KeyId(key, "req") is int requestId)
        {
            OpenRequest(requestId);
            return;
        }

        if (KeyId(key, "ptask") is int taskId
            && _personal.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == taskId) is { } own)
        {
            OpenTask(own);
        }
    }

    private async Task OnActivityKeyAsync(string key)
    {
        var rows = Activity;
        if (KeyId(key, "act") is int i && i >= 0 && i < rows.Count)
            await OpenActivityAsync(rows[i]);
    }

    // ── Attention ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>The shared waiting phrase for one request, when it is currently
    /// on this mentor. Null hides the chip inside MentorRequestDetail, which is
    /// correct for a request the lecturer or the team is holding.</summary>
    private string? WaitingLabelFor(int requestId) =>
        _attention.FirstOrDefault(i => i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Request
                                       && i.EntityId == requestId)?.WaitingLabel;

    // ── Work tabs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // The tab pills, their badges and their "all" links moved into
    // WorkTabViews above — one place now states a tab's label, its count and
    // where it hands off to, instead of four members that had to agree.

    private void OpenRequest(int requestId) =>
        _openRequestId = _openRequestId == requestId ? null : requestId;

    private void CloseRequest() => _openRequestId = null;

    /// <summary>The row behind the open request id — the surface's header is
    /// built from the SAME snapshot row the section drew, so the title, the
    /// type and the status on the surface cannot disagree with the row that
    /// opened it.</summary>
    private ProjectRequestRowDto? RequestRow(int id) =>
        _requests.FirstOrDefault(r => r.Id == id);

    /// <summary>Who filed it, when, and how long it has been waiting — the
    /// three facts the title and the status do not carry. The waiting phrase
    /// comes from the shared attention model and is present only while the
    /// request is genuinely on this mentor.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PwMeta> RequestMeta(ProjectRequestRowDto r)
    {
        var meta = new List<PwMeta>();

        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(r.CreatedByName))
            meta.Add(new PwMeta(r.CreatedByName!, "oi-person"));

        meta.Add(new PwMeta($"נפתחה {r.CreatedAt.ToLocalTime():dd.MM.yyyy}", "oi-clock"));

        if (WaitingLabelFor(r.Id) is { Length: > 0 } waiting)
            meta.Add(new PwMeta(waiting));

        return meta;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One deliverable, in the four facts the section actually draws.
    ///
    /// <para><paramref name="Due"/> reaches the row only when
    /// <paramref name="Overdue"/> is true — a date that was met is not news.
    /// <paramref name="Submitted"/> is "the team has handed something in at
    /// least once", which is both the row's rank and what the section's summary
    /// counts when nothing is waiting on this mentor.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>The milestone is the row's CONTEXT LINE. It came off the row when
    /// the row was one line and the milestone was its fourth competing fact; a
    /// two-line row has somewhere to put it, and "which milestone is this
    /// deliverable for" is the one thing a title alone does not say.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private sealed record SubRow(
        string Title, string Milestone, string State, string StateClass,
        int? SubmissionId, string Due, bool Overdue, bool Submitted);

    /// <summary>
    /// Every deliverable on the project, in milestone order.
    ///
    /// <para>The rows are the project's own submission TASKS, and the review id
    /// is attached from <c>PendingSubmissions</c> — the only place a submission
    /// id reaches this page. A task with no pending round therefore carries no
    /// button, which is honest: its history lives one call deeper, inside the
    /// review surface, and there is no id here to open it with.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Which of these the section DRAWS is decided by
    /// <see cref="SubmissionRank"/>, not here — this list stays complete so the
    /// "לכל ההגשות" disclosure and the summary counts have something to read.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<SubRow> Submissions
    {
        get
        {
            if (_detail is null) return Array.Empty<SubRow>();

            var pending = _detail.PendingSubmissions.ToDictionary(s => s.TaskId, s => s.SubmissionId);

            return _detail.Milestones
                .OrderBy(m => m.OrderIndex)
                .SelectMany(m => m.Tasks.Where(t => t.IsSubmission).Select(t => (Milestone: m, Task: t)))
                .Select(x =>
                {
                    var t = x.Task;
                    int? id = pending.TryGetValue(t.Id, out var subId) ? subId : null;

                    var (state, cls) =
                        // The mentor's own review queue. It was keyed "mpw-late"
                        // and therefore drew rose — the same mis-assignment the
                        // lecturer's "ממתין לאישורך" carried. Nothing here is
                        // past a deadline; it is waiting on the reader.
                        id is not null                    ? ("ממתין לבדיקה שלך", "mpw-state-attention")
                        : t.LatestMentorStatus == "Approved" ? ("נבדק ואושר", "mpw-state-teal")
                        : t.LatestMentorStatus == "Returned" ? ("הוחזר לתיקון", "mpw-state-violet")
                        : t.LatestSubmissionStatus is not null ? ("הוגש", "mpw-state-blue")
                        : t.IsOverdue                        ? ("טרם הוגש · באיחור", "mpw-late")
                        :                                      ("טרם הוגש", "mpw-state-quiet");

                    return new SubRow(t.Title, x.Milestone.Title, state, cls, id,
                                      PwDates.DueLabel(t.DueDate), t.IsOverdue,
                                      t.LatestSubmissionStatus is not null);
                })
                // Milestone order, and only milestone order. What comes first on
                // the card is decided by PwRowRank now, and OrderBy is stable, so
                // this ordering survives inside each rank.
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    /// <summary><paramref name="Task"/> is the mentor's own personal task when
    /// the row is one, and null for a team task. It replaced an
    /// <c>Href</c> to /mentor/tasks?editTask=: the row now opens the shared
    /// editor over this workspace rather than navigating to המשימות שלי to open
    /// the same modal there. A team task stays unclickable — this page has no
    /// editor for one.</summary>
    private sealed record WorkTaskRow(
        bool IsMine, string Title, string Assignee, string Due, bool Overdue,
        string State, string StateClass, PersonalTaskDto? Task);

    /// <summary>
    /// The open work on this project, from both sides of it: the team's own
    /// tasks (from the project payload) and the mentor's personal tasks
    /// associated with it (from the shared snapshot). Overdue first, then by
    /// deadline — a mentor scanning this wants the slipping row at the top.
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<WorkTaskRow> WorkTasks
    {
        get
        {
            var rows = new List<WorkTaskRow>();

            if (_detail is not null)
            {
                // SUBMISSION TASKS ARE EXCLUDED, as they already were on the
                // lecturer's workspace. A deliverable is the הגשות section; listing
                // it again here put the same row on the page twice, with two
                // different states, under two different headings.
                foreach (var t in _detail.Milestones
                             .SelectMany(m => m.Tasks)
                             .Where(t => !t.IsSubmission
                                         && t.Status is not ("Done" or "Completed" or "ApprovedForSubmission")))
                {
                    rows.Add(new WorkTaskRow(
                        IsMine:     false,
                        Title:      t.Title,
                        Assignee:   string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(t.AssignedToName) ? "—" : t.AssignedToName,
                        Due:        DueLabel(t.DueDate),
                        Overdue:    t.IsOverdue,
                        State:      TaskStatusLabel(t),
                        StateClass: TaskStateClass(t),
                        Task:       null));
                }
            }

            foreach (var t in _personal.Where(t => !t.IsDone))
            {
                bool overdue = MentorTime.IsOverdue(t.DueDate);
                rows.Add(new WorkTaskRow(
                    IsMine:     true,
                    Title:      t.Title,
                    Assignee:   "משימה שלך",
                    Due:        DueLabel(t.DueDate),
                    Overdue:    overdue,
                    State:      overdue ? "באיחור" : "פתוחה",
                    StateClass: overdue ? "mpw-late" : "mpw-state-quiet",
                    // The mentor's own task opens its editor — the same shared
                    // modal the calendar and המשימות שלי open, mounted here.
                    Task:       t));
            }

            // Overdue first inside the rank the card sorts by; PwRowRank makes
            // the same row first on the card, and this keeps the tie-break the
            // page has always used.
            return rows
                .OrderByDescending(r => r.Overdue)
                .ThenBy(r => r.Due == "—" ? 1 : 0)
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    private static string DueLabel(DateTime? due)
    {
        if (due is null) return "—";
        var d = due.Value.ToLocalTime().Date;
        if (d == DateTime.Today)            return "היום";
        if (d == DateTime.Today.AddDays(1)) return "מחר";
        return d.ToString("dd.MM");
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The state key for a TEAM task's pill.
    ///
    /// <para><b>Lateness no longer overrides the state word.</b> This opened
    /// with <c>if (t.IsOverdue) return "mpw-late"</c>, which painted a rose
    /// pill over a label reading "בביצוע" — a colour saying "problem" on a
    /// word saying "in progress". The row already states the lateness twice
    /// and truthfully: its due date renders rose (Overdue), and the section
    /// summary counts "N משימות באיחור" in rose. The pill states the workflow
    /// state, which is what a pill is for.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Nothing about ordering moves: TaskRank reads <c>k.Overdue</c>
    /// directly, so an overdue task is still the card's first row.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>The mentor's OWN tasks keep their rose pill, and that is not an
    /// inconsistency — their label literally reads "באיחור", so there the
    /// colour and the word agree.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string TaskStateClass(MentorTaskDto t)
    {

        return t.Status switch
        {
            "SubmittedToMentor" or "RevisionSubmitted" => "mpw-state-blue",
            "ReturnedForRevision"                      => "mpw-state-violet",
            "InProgress"                               => "mpw-state-blue",
            _                                          => "mpw-state-quiet",
        };
    }

    // ── Dates and meetings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The last guidance meeting that actually happened.
    ///
    /// <para>Read straight from the project's personal tasks rather than from
    /// the composed calendar, because that composer deliberately drops COMPLETED
    /// entries — right for a planner, wrong for "when did we last meet". Same
    /// definition of a meeting either way: a project entry with an hour someone
    /// chose.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private string LastMeetingLabel
    {
        get
        {
            var last = _personal
                .Where(t => t.DueDate is DateTime d && d.Date < DateTime.Today
                            && MotivaDates.ParseWallClock(t.StartTime) is not null)
                .OrderByDescending(t => t.DueDate!.Value)
                .FirstOrDefault();

            return last is null
                ? "טרם התקיימה פגישת הנחיה"
                : $"פגישה אחרונה: {last.DueDate!.Value:dd.MM} · {last.Title}";
        }
    }

    private void OpenScheduler() => _scheduleOpen = true;

    /// <summary>The shared editor, opened over this workspace.</summary>
    private void OpenTask(PersonalTaskDto task) => _editingTask = task;

    private void CloseTaskModal()
    {
        _scheduleOpen = false;
        _editingTask  = null;
    }

    private async Task OnTaskRemovedAsync()
    {
        CloseTaskModal();
        await LoadAsync();
    }

    // ── Opening an entity, in place ─────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // THE RULE, AND WHY THIS PAGE OBEYS IT TOO. A click on an entity inside an
    // overview list INSPECTS it where the reader already is; only an explicit
    // CTA navigates. This screen is a destination, but its lists are overviews
    // of the same four kinds — and every one of them used to be an href that
    // moved the mentor somewhere else in order to open a panel. The submission
    // case was the plainest: the row re-navigated THIS route with
    // ?submissionId= on it, remounting the page to open a drawer that was
    // already there.
    //
    // Nothing about the destinations changed. Every one of them is still
    // reachable, from the CTA inside whatever this opens.

    /// <summary>One attention row, opened in whichever surface owns its kind.</summary>
    private async Task OpenAttentionItemAsync(MentorAttentionItemDto item)
    {
        switch (item.Kind)
        {
            case MentorAttentionKind.Submission:
                await OpenReviewDrawer(item.EntityId);
                break;

            // The request's own surface — the same MentorRequestDetail the
            // inbox draws, with the same one POST.
            case MentorAttentionKind.Request when _requests.Any(r => r.Id == item.EntityId):
                OpenRequest(item.EntityId);
                break;

            case MentorAttentionKind.PersonalTask
                 when _personal.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == item.EntityId) is { } own:
                OpenTask(own);
                break;

            // A kind this page has no surface for keeps the link it always had.
            default:
                Nav.NavigateTo(item.Href);
                break;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>One activity row. Same routing as an attention row, on the
    /// entity the entry was built from; Href is the fallback for an entry this
    /// page cannot open itself.</summary>
    private async Task OpenActivityAsync(ActivityRow row)
    {
        if (row.Kind is MentorAttentionKind kind)
        {
            await OpenAttentionItemAsync(new MentorAttentionItemDto
            {
                Kind     = kind,
                EntityId = row.EntityId,
                Href     = row.Href,
            });
            return;
        }

        Nav.NavigateTo(row.Href);
    }

    private async Task OnMeetingSavedAsync(PersonalTaskDto _)
    {
        CloseTaskModal();
        await ReloadAsync();
    }

    // ── Recent activity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary><paramref name="Kind"/> and <paramref name="EntityId"/> are
    /// what the row actually points AT, so clicking it can open that entity in
    /// place through the same routing an attention row uses.
    /// <paramref name="Href"/> stays as the fallback destination for a row this
    /// page has no surface for, and as the CTA a popup then offers.</summary>
    private sealed record ActivityRow(
        DateTime When, string Text, string Meta, string Href, string ToneClass,
        MentorAttentionKind? Kind = null, int EntityId = 0);

    /// <summary>
    /// Only events this page does not already state somewhere else.
    ///
    /// <para>"בקשה נפתחה — X" IS GONE. It was the largest source of lines here
    /// and every one of them named a request that is a row in the בקשות
    /// section, carrying its own status and its own filing date. The feed was
    /// re-reading the page to the reader.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>What is left is what nothing else says: a request that MOVED
    /// after it was filed (the section shows where it is, never when it last
    /// changed), a submission ARRIVING (the section shows the deliverable's
    /// state, never who handed it in), and a guidance meeting that has already
    /// happened — the only past event on this page at all, and one the header
    /// summarises to a single "last meeting" line.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Still no fifth source: milestone completion, task creation and
    /// review decisions store no project-scoped timestamp anywhere, so they
    /// are absent rather than guessed.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<ActivityRow> Activity
    {
        get
        {
            var rows = new List<ActivityRow>();

            // Only the MOVE, never the opening — the opening is the row in בקשות.
            foreach (var r in _requests.Where(r => r.UpdatedAt.Date != r.CreatedAt.Date
                                                   || r.UpdatedAt > r.CreatedAt.AddMinutes(1)))
            {
                rows.Add(new ActivityRow(
                    r.UpdatedAt, $"עדכון בבקשה — {r.Title}",
                    $"{PwRequestVocabulary.StatusLabel(r.Status, ViewerOf(r))} · {r.UpdatedAt.ToLocalTime():dd.MM}",
                    $"{MentorLinks.RequestsInbox}?requestId={r.Id}", "mpw-dot-violet",
                    MentorAttentionKind.Request, r.Id));
            }

            if (_detail is not null)
            {
                foreach (var s in _detail.PendingSubmissions)
                {
                    // The attention model already owns the deep link to this
                    // submission's review drawer; the queue is the fallback for a
                    // row that is somehow not in attention.
                    var href = _attention
                        .FirstOrDefault(i => i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Submission
                                             && i.EntityId == s.SubmissionId)?.Href;

                    rows.Add(new ActivityRow(
                        s.SubmittedAt, $"הגשה התקבלה — {s.TaskTitle}",
                        $"{s.SubmittedBy} · {s.SubmittedAt.ToLocalTime():dd.MM}",
                        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(href) ? MentorLinks.Reviews : href!,
                        "mpw-dot-blue", MentorAttentionKind.Submission, s.SubmissionId));
                }
            }

            foreach (var t in _personal.Where(t => t.DueDate is DateTime d && d.Date < DateTime.Today
                                                   && MotivaDates.ParseWallClock(t.StartTime) is not null))
            {
                rows.Add(new ActivityRow(
                    t.DueDate!.Value, $"פגישת הנחיה התקיימה — {t.Title}",
                    $"{t.DueDate.Value:dd.MM} · {t.StartTime}",
                    MentorLinks.PersonalTask(t.Id), "mpw-dot-teal",
                    MentorAttentionKind.PersonalTask, t.Id));
            }

            return rows.OrderByDescending(r => r.When).Take(5).ToList();
        }
    }

    // ── Review drawer: open / close / submit (unchanged flow) ───────────────

    /// <summary>One query value by name, or null. Mirrors the reader
    /// MentorTasksPage uses for its own deep link — one shape, no parser
    /// dependency this project does not already carry.</summary>
    private string? QueryValue(string key)
    {
        var query = new Uri(Nav.Uri).Query.TrimStart('?');

        foreach (var pair in query.Split('&', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries))
        {
            var eq = pair.IndexOf('=');
            if (eq <= 0) continue;
            if (!pair.AsSpan(0, eq).Equals(key, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) continue;
            return Uri.UnescapeDataString(pair[(eq + 1)..]);
        }

        return null;
    }

    private async Task OpenReviewDrawer(int submissionId)
    {
        _reviewOpen     = true;
        _reviewCtx      = null;
        _reviewFeedback = "";
        _reviewError    = false;
        _feedbackError  = "";
        _reviewLoading  = true;
        StateHasChanged();

        _reviewCtx     = await MentorService.GetSubmissionContextAsync(submissionId);
        _reviewLoading = false;

        StateHasChanged();
    }

    private void CloseDrawer()
    {
        _reviewOpen     = false;
        _reviewCtx      = null;
        _reviewFeedback = "";
        _reviewError    = false;
        _feedbackError  = "";
    }

    private async Task SubmitReviewAsync(string action)
    {
        if (_reviewCtx is null || _reviewing) return;

        // Validation: returning for correction requires a non-empty note.
        // Backend enforces the same rule with the identical Hebrew message —
        // this branch just avoids the round-trip when we can see it locally.
        if (action == "Returned" && string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewFeedback))
        {
            _feedbackError = "יש להזין הערת מנחה לפני החזרת ההגשה לתיקון";
            StateHasChanged();
            return;
        }

        _reviewing     = true;
        _pendingAction = action;
        _reviewError   = false;
        _feedbackError = "";
        StateHasChanged();

        bool ok = await MentorService.ReviewSubmissionAsync(
            _reviewCtx.SubmissionId, action, _reviewFeedback);

        _reviewing = false;

        if (ok)
        {
            // Optimistically update the drawer, then reload — the decision moves
            // the item out of attention, off the tiles and out of the הגשות
            // badge, and every one of those is derived rather than stored here.
            _reviewCtx.MentorStatus   = action;
            _reviewCtx.MentorFeedback = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewFeedback) ? null : _reviewFeedback;

            await LoadAsync();
        }
        else
        {
            _reviewError = true;
        }

        StateHasChanged();
    }

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private static string TaskStatusLabel(MentorTaskDto task)
    {
        if (task.IsSubmission && task.LatestMentorStatus == "Pending"
            && task.Status == "ReturnedForRevision")
            return "הוגש מחדש";

        return task.Status switch
        {
            "Open"                  => "פתוח",
            "InProgress"            => "בביצוע",
            "SubmittedToMentor"     => "הוגש למנחה",
            "ReturnedForRevision"   => "הוחזר לתיקון",
            "RevisionSubmitted"     => "תיקון הוגש",
            "ApprovedForSubmission" => "אושר להגשה",
            "Done" or "Completed"   => "הושלם",
            _                       => task.Status,
        };
    }

    /// <summary>Who and when, for the review surface's header. Empty while the
    /// context is still loading, which is when the surface has no facts to
    /// state yet.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PwMeta> ReviewMeta =>
        _reviewCtx is null
            ? Array.Empty<PwMeta>()
            : new[]
              {
                  new PwMeta(_reviewCtx.SubmittedBy, "oi-person"),
                  new PwMeta(_reviewCtx.SubmittedAt.IsraelFormat(), "oi-clock"),
              };

    /// <summary>THE DRIVE LINK COUNTS AS A FILE. Submissions have been
    /// Drive-link only since 2026-05-19, so a count of `Files` alone reports
    /// zero for every modern submission — while the link to the deliverable
    /// sits in the same payload.</summary>
    private int ReviewFileCount =>
        (_reviewCtx?.Files.Count ?? 0)
        + (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_reviewCtx?.DriveUrl) ? 0 : 1);

    /// <summary>The mentor decision in the shared five-tone scale — the same
    /// vocabulary a request's status badge uses on the same surface.</summary>
    /// <summary>The review drawer's own status, in the shared vocabulary.
    /// "Returned" was rose: sending work back to a team is a normal step of the
    /// review, not a failure, so it takes the Waiting rung the row it came from
    /// takes. Pending is the reader's queue — Attention.</summary>
    private static PwTone ReviewTone(string s) => s switch
    {
        "Approved" => PwTone.Done,
        "Returned" => PwTone.Waiting,
        _          => PwTone.Attention,
    };

    private static string ReviewToneClass(string s) => ReviewTone(s) switch
    {
        PwTone.Done    => "pwd-tone-done",
        PwTone.Waiting => "pwd-tone-waiting",
        _              => "pwd-tone-attention",
    };

    private static string DrawerMentorStatusLabel(string s) => s switch
    {
        "Approved" => "אושר",
        "Returned" => "הוחזר לתיקון",
        _          => "ממתין לאישורך",
    };

    private static string FileIcon(string contentType)
    {
        if (contentType.StartsWith("image/"))   return "oi-image";
        if (contentType == "application/pdf")   return "oi-document";
        if (contentType.Contains("word"))       return "oi-document";
        if (contentType.Contains("zip") || contentType.Contains("compressed")) return "oi-layers";
        return "oi-file";
    }

    private static string FormatSize(long bytes)
    {
        if (bytes < 1024)           return $"{bytes} B";
        if (bytes < 1024 * 1024)    return $"{bytes / 1024.0:F1} KB";
        return $"{bytes / (1024.0 * 1024):F1} MB";
    }
